From 526dda36ecc8ba9fb9790727b01b7f2a9c4fc1f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:00:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): clean the Doosan DNM header name and refuse
 O-numbers past O9999

onOpen wrote the machine name into the header comment as it came. A
name such as "DNM 5700 (5AX)" gave nested parentheses, and a % in the
name ended the tape. The name now goes through the post's clean(), as
in fanuc.cps and fanuc-lathe.cps (#594).

oWord() clamped a program number above 9999 to O9999, which is another
program. It now refuses a number outside O0001-O9999 by name, with the
fanuc.cps text. A number of 0 is refused too; it no longer becomes
O0001.

Pinned by doosan_dnm_header_cleans_the_name_and_refuses_a_number_past_o9999
and by doosan-dnm in hostile_names_post_well_formed_comments_in_every_mill_dialect.

Fixes #4349

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
